# scripts/opcount: `llmbench bench fold N` folds N text deltas, in replies
# of 64, with llm.Fold (wf10 L1); the cost of one delta is the slope
# between the two sizes. The control is hand Go: the same deltas as a
# tagged struct, folded by a switch that appends each text to one buffer.
# The floor appends each word straight to the buffer: no delta value.
unit delta
sizes 409600 2457600
args bench fold {n}
control benchmarks/llm/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/llm/testdata/floor
